# Elegy Acolyte's Void, second clause: "a spell was warped this turn" (CR 702.185c) - a spell cast for its warp cost.
# Turn 1 puts the Acolyte out with no departure (no Robot, as in the first scenario). Turn 3 Bot1 does nothing but warp
# Pinnacle Emissary (paid with the Mox Ruby): nothing has left the battlefield at the beginning of the end step, when
# the Void "if" is checked, so only the warp makes it true. The Robot token is created, and the warped Emissary is
# exiled by its own end-step trigger (it left the battlefield only after Void's condition had been satisfied).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Dark Ritual
Mox Ruby
Elegy Acolyte
Pinnacle Emissary
Island x2
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dark Ritual.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Elegy Acolyte.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Elegy Acolyte
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Pinnacle Emissary.Cast(Ability: Warp)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Mox Ruby; Elegy Acolyte; Robot Token
Exile = Pinnacle Emissary
Bot1.Battlefield.Robot Token.Token = true
